    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 4th slate with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns today\u2019s highest efficiency mark at 80.98. His favorable matchup against Leahy and a prime spot at the top of the order provide a significant boost, though **Christian Yelich** follows closely with a 75.84 score. **Christian Yelich** benefits immensely from the matchup against Kelly and his park-adjusted metrics, easily offsetting a minor BvP penalty. While **Yordan Alvarez** maintains his status as our primary power threat, his relatively lower score of 55.68 reflects the difficulty of his matchup against a high-skill arm like Rasmussen, emphasizing our commitment to maximizing efficiency in the categories of SB and AVG over raw power alone.\n\nRegarding our bench strategy, **Luke Raley** was the most difficult exclusion of the day, missing the cut with a 59.03 score. Despite a favorable xERA from the opposing pitcher, **Luke Raley** was relegated to the bench because the cumulative efficiency of our outfield and utility starters\u2014specifically the high-upside plays of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Christian Yelich**\u2014simply offered a higher statistical floor for our 5x5 objectives. We are also monitoring a 40% rain risk affecting **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**; both players are locked into their spots due to high projected value, but managers should keep an eye on potential in-game delays in their respective contests. **Kazuma Okamoto** rounds out our lineup, though his 42.64 score against a tough arm in Gilbert suggests he remains a volatile piece today, requiring immediate replacement if any late-scratch news arises regarding our higher-priority options.",
